wiring.phext - the ranch network, declared
==========================================

This file is the declaration of record for the Bickford Llama Ranch
fleet network: what is wired to what, what addresses the links
carry, which proxy each set of machines uses, and how packets are
routed. Will audits this file. Emise enforces it: the checker
(~/workspace/ranch-network-fix/check_wiring.py) parses this file
through libphext, probes the live fleet, and reports every place
reality departs from what is declared here. A departure that is
known and accepted is written into the divergence register
(1.1.1/1.1.1/4.1.1) with its reason - a recorded divergence is how
an exception stays honest instead of becoming invisible drift.

Home of record: wbic16/human@exo (human.git), at the repository
root. Working copy: ~/workspace/phext/wiring.phext. This file is
the artifact - there is no hidden source behind it. Edit it
directly; the checker reads what is written here.

The rulings this file encodes (Will, 2026-11-21):
- 10:36 CST - each set of machines targets a separate proxy, so
  transfers do not starve on one shared proxy.
- 10:40 CST - routing is configured so packets route efficiently
  between nodes, over the best direct path.
- 10:40 CST - WiFi is back-haul of last resort, so SSH terminals
  from Will's laptop are not clogged.
- 10:40 CST - SSH traffic to and from lilly (Will's laptop) has
  top priority on any shared path.
- 10:54 CST - every row has two 2.5G Ethernet uplinks and USB4
  interlinks.
- 11:15 CST - this file: a config Will can audit and Emise can
  enforce.

Sets are the six rows of the wiring diagram Will posted
2026-11-21. (The groups-of-5 roster he mentioned was not found
in any record; the rows are the physical sets the diagram itself
draws, and the census derived the same sets.)

