Sources this declaration was built from (verified records only):
~/workspace/ranch-network-fix/TOPOLOGY.md (the diagram, as
corrected by Will's 10:54 ruling), INTERIM.md (the 2026-11-21
census), and USB4-STATE.md (the USB4 configuration as built).
Conventions - how to read and edit this file
============================================

Coordinates in this file: chapter 1 is the front matter, chapter
2 is the grid (section = row), chapter 3 is policy, chapter 4 is
the divergence register, chapter 5 is reserved for external and
inbound links (see 1.1.1/1.1.1/5.1.1). One scroll per subject; a
scroll is a page of plain text and reads top to bottom.

Machine-checked lines: the checker reads lines that begin with
"node:", "usb4:", "xlink:", "uplink:", "proxy:", "metric:", and
"divergence:". Everything else is prose for the human auditor.
Keep those lines in their declared forms when editing; the forms
are:

node: <INITIALS> <hostname|unknown> col <1-4> ram <GB> state <state> ssh <tailnet-ip|->
usb4: <A>-<B> subnet <10.54.x.0/24> <A> <ip> <B> <ip> expect-gbit 10-40
xlink: <A>-<B> subnet <10.54.9x.0/24> <A> <ip> <B> <ip> expect-gbit 10-40 state <status>
uplink: <left|right> <INITIALS> <iface|unknown>
proxy: host <INITIALS> port 3129
metric: <ethernet|usb4|wifi> <number>
divergence: <D#> keys <key[,...]> - <statement and reason>

Node states: online (SSH-verified on the tailnet), dark (powered
off or idle; not probed), unlocated (drawn on the diagram; no
hostname or address found in any record), key-refused (the node
exists, but does not accept Emise's SSH key).

USB4 addressing (from USB4-STATE.md, as built): static per-link
/24s from 10.54.0.0/16 - outside the LAN (192.168.86.0/24) and
outside the retired 10.53 tbfab block. An in-row link between
columns c and c+1 of row r takes subnet 10.54.<r><c>.0/24; the
left node is .1, the right node is .2. Cross-row and off-diagram
links take the 10.54.9x.0/24 block. MTU 1500.

Route metrics (policy, see 1.1.1/1.1.1/3.1.1): ethernet 100,
USB4 200, WiFi 600. Lower wins; WiFi carries traffic only when
no wired path exists.

Proxy convention (policy, see 1.1.1/1.1.1/3.2.1): each row's
proxy host is the row's left-edge (column 1) uplink node,
serving Squid on port 3129 - the port the fleet's client
configs already use for HTTPS (3128 is its plain-HTTP
companion). Row 5 is the standing exception: AM is unlocated,
so quacked-hill (column 4) acts as row 5's proxy host until AM
is found. A row proxy must not ssl-bump with a CA whose
certificates fail fleet verification (the legacy proxy's
defect; see divergence D11).

The diagram's node colors (blue, red, gold) have no verified
correlate - the census tested status, Thunderbolt state, CPU
batch, RAM, and role. They are carried in no declaration here;
see divergence D14.
